Z||000010||Fformula88||02-11-2001||05:20 PM||||After checking out the GT, I've decided to keep the Formula.  The frame and body are not in as good of shape as those on my Formula.  The interior is near mint, while mine would be if it wasn't for the seats.  Nothing some nice covers won't fix!  The engine seems to be good, but it has more miles than my car.<P>Thanks for the offer for help.  I cannot be totally sure the problems are related to the engine/trans or not.  At idle while cold (but sometimes warm also) the car idles very bad and will stall.  It will also stall when put into reverse a lot.  Other times the car runs perfect.  Temperature, humidity or weather seems to have no effect.  Vacumn in the engine is good, IAC, throttle and intake have been cleaned.  I was told the injectors are good.  New EGR valve, EGR tube without any help.  I am out of ideas.  I had it out today and it ran perfectly.  But this has happened before and the problems will return.  Hope this helps.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mi Junk||02-12-2001||12:10 AM||||Have you checked the EGR solenoid.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||02-12-2001||05:23 PM||||I think this is starting to belong in the tech forum, but were here now!  I did replace the vacumn lines to and from the solenoid.  I didn't replace it, but my understanding of its operation is that it won't have much of an affect at idle, if any.  Thats where the problem is.  Unless I misunderstand it, the soleniod only operates the valve when the car is at speed, but at idle it keeps the valve closed (it doesn't send the vacumn pulses to the valve).  If I am wrong CORRECT ME PLEASE!  LOL.  Thanks!||||reg||1
